   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Find the value of \\( \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{(2 + h)^{3} - 8}{h} \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 12
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The numerator has the form \\( f(2 + h) - f(2) \\) with \\( f(x) = x^{3} \\), because \\( f(2) = 8 \\).",
         "mathjson": 8
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "So the function is \\( f(x) = x^{3} \\) and the base point is \\( x = 2 \\).",
         "mathjson": 2
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The limit is the definition of \\( f'(2) \\), and \\( f'(x) = 3 x^{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            3,
            [
               "Power",
               "x",
               2
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "Evaluate: \\( f'(2) = 12 \\).",
         "mathjson": 12
      }
   ],
